welcome back to the David Pakman show  happening now or at least at the time of  this recording Attorney General William  Barr is testifying before the before  Congress and we got it we obtained a  clip of Barr refusing to answer the  question of whether or not the White  House itself actually saw the Muller  report now you can recall everyone knows  the Muller report was a 22 month process  an investigation and instead of  releasing the report William Barr  released a four-page summary and Donald  Trump said that this summary exonerated  him completely or rather he said that  the report exonerated him completely but  representative needle owie  asked asked William Barnes just a moment  ago did the White House see the report  before you released your summarizing  letter has the White House seen it since  have they been briefed on the contents  beyond what was your summarizing letter  and bar refused to answer let's take a  quick look at this clip that's did the  White House see the report before you  released your summarizing letter has the  White House seen it since then  have they been briefed on the contents  beyond what was in you a summarizing  letter to the Judiciary Committee I've  said what I'm going to say about the  report today I've three letters about it  and I was willing to discuss the  historic information of how the report  came to me in my decision on Sunday but  I've already laid out the process that  is going forward to release these  reports hopefully within a week and I'm  not going to say anything more about it  until the report is out and everyone has  a chance to look at it so Attorney  General Barr is making it clear that  this is a question that he cannot answer  IIIi don't you know we can parse it  however you want to parse it but he  refuses to answer this and this is  important because this cut to this cuts  to what we discussed in a previous  segment where  Donald Trump set the narrative by saying  he's been fully exonerated media outlets  picked up this narrative spread it  around as though it was absolutely the  fact matter of fact also as though  they've read the summary or rather read  the Mullah report themselves well now it  turns out it sounds like the President  of the United States himself has not  read the report or anyone in the White  House the question was a general  question did the White House see the  report and I just did Donald Trump see  the report but did the White House see  the report and the bar was not willing  to answer something else that we can  glean from this brief exchange is the  fact that it looks as though they are  gearing up to release the report because  of all the pressure that's being mounted  against them the attempt to keep this as  private as they possibly could it looks  as though they're going to have to  release the report the question is how  much of the report will be redacted  right how much of the White House how  much is the White House going to redact  it so at some point whether or not Trump  has seen it yet they're going to see it  and they're going to be given the  opportunity to redact as much  information as they would like  well if Donald Trump was completely  exonerated then by all means release the  entire report this is the frustrating  part about journalism about media about  politics in general we needed the media  to do their job and to point out these  inconsistencies and the glaring  hypocrisy of us having to take at face  value a summary versus the full report  right we who else is going to hold  political power accountable if the media  is not and while the media took the last  several weeks to slam dunk on MSNBC  probably rightfully so will it still  remains to be seen  right to slam dunk on everyone who  believed that there was anything to the  Russia probe at all they should have  been pointing out the fact that we have  not seen the report too concretely and  to definitively say that  Donald Trump has been exonerated what  they did instead was take the  president's word for it and use that for  a new cycle in which they lambasted  anyone who believed anything about the  Russia probe whatsoever and now it turns  out that it looks as though that the  White House itself has not seen the full  report or has not read the full report  at least according to the exchange that  we just saw between bar and Congress  person LOI this this is just another  another another important point in a  series of important points that shows  you several things that shows you that  the President of the United States  absolutely does have something to hide  whether or not it is it is impeachable  we see you know that that is a political  question right that is a political  question in terms of whether or not it  met the legal bar to indict him we see  that it did not meet the legal bar to  indict him according to robert muller  but we also know that there's been this  that there's been indictable offences or  rather there's been impeachable offenses  that have not met the indictment bar so  you know I I for one if you go back to  my catalogue of videos my number one  thing always was hey let's let this play  out let's let the mullet probe play  itself out and see what information we  get from it and here we've let allowed  it to play out at least I have without  you know most of us have done it without  jumping on the bandwagon of the the  hysteria but at the same time not  dismissing it you know there's an entire  contingency of  so-called objective journalists who have  been dismissing it and have taken an  active role in dismissing the entire  malla probe as nothing more than  conspiracy and yet here we have the  Attorney General of the United States of  America saying well first of all being a  barrier to sing in the full report and  now saying that we don't even know if  the White House has read the report  where are the journalists who are going  to say hold up wait a minute there's  something going on here that we need to  get to the bottom of I don't know  they're too busy slam dunking because  you know we the report did not prove  that Donald Trump was an actual  Manchurian Candidate being controlled by  Russia and because he wasn't an actual  mentor in candidate being controlled by  Russia then there's nothing to see here  well there's still some smoke here and  the smoke is the fact that Barr was  placed into position to block this  report from coming out and it did  exactly what he was there to do which  was to muddy the waters enough for a new  cycle long enough for us to get to the  point where we move on from it and now  the rest of this is just kind of  secondary conversations

